title: Algorithm – List Processing

files:
  - em.prog:em.benchmark.coremark/ListBench.em.ts
  - .assets/img-102-05-01.png
  - .assets/img-102-05-02.png

steps:
  - cmds:
      - view 2
    text: |
      {[ht,$start]%[cu]ListBench% Algorithm}

      The last **CoreMark** algorithm features typical *list process&shy;ing* operations, and plays a special role in the benchmark.

      The {[cu]ListBench} module tracks `core_list_join.c`, while also implementing the common {[cu]BenchAlgI} interface.

      Unlike its sibling modules, the {[cu]CoreBench} um&shy;brella *only* calls {[cu]ListBench}.{[cf]run} when executing the benchmark.

      {[in]%[cu]CoreBench% also bound %[cu]ListBench%.%[cn]Board&lbrack;01&rbrack;% proxies to %[cu]StateBench% and %[cu]MatrixBench% at build-time.}

      Before examining its more complex codebase, we'll first introduce some key internal elements of {[cu]ListBench}.

  - cmds:
      - view 3
    text: |
      {[ht,$peek]%[cu]ListBench% Codescape}

      {[bm,1]} This module enapsulates a singly-linked list containing {[ct]Elem} and {[ct]Data} nodes; the latter type holds two numbers.

      {[bm,2]} {[cu]ListBench}.{[cf]setup} seeds each {[ct]Data} node with two numbers and points {[cn]cur_head} at the list's first {[ct]Elem}.

      {[bm,3]} {[cu]ListBench}.{[cf]run} uses helpers to re-arrange the list.

      {[bm,4]} The {[cf]find} helper locates {[ct]Data} nodes by {[cn]idx} or {[cn]val}.

      {[bm,5]} A generic {[cf]sort} function abstracts list ordering by re&shy;ceiving a callback conforming to the {[ct]Comparator} type.

      {[bm,6]} The {[cf]idxCompare}{[ct]Comparator} sorts by {[ct]Data}.{[cn]idx}.

      {[bm,7]} Using <i>other</i>&thinsp;{[ct]BenchI} modules, {[cf]valCompare} sorts the list using a calculated value dervied from each {[ct]Data} node.

  - cmds:
      - close 2
      - open 1
      - mark 1 A 8
      - mark 1 B 10
      - mark 1 C 13
      - mark 1 D 18
      - mark 1 E 20
    focus: [1, 1]
    text: |
      {[ht,$details]%[cu]ListBench% &ndash; static declarations}

  - cmds:
      - open 1
      - mark 1 A 8
      - mark 1 B 10
      - mark 1 C 13
      - mark 1 D 18
      - mark 1 E 20
